-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Follows details about the updated castor->

Reasons->IGI when performed pen test of their product, they are reported with following vulnerability in castor which SDI belong.
castor-0.9.5.4-xml.jar 	/src/opt/ibm/SDI1/V7.2/jars/3rdparty/others/castor-0.9.5.4-xml.jar 	 CVE-2014-3004 	MEDIUM

Vulnerability details can be found in the below links->

https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2014-3004

https://cve.mitre.org/cgi-bin/cvename.cgi?name=CVE-2014-3004

The vulnrability says that

The default configuration for the Xerces SAX Parser in Castor before 1.3.3 allows context-dependent attackers to conduct XML External Entity (XXE) attacks via a crafted XML document. 

What we did ->

Attempt  [1] -> To fix the vulnerability we tried to upgrade the castor libraries to the version 1.4.1.

But it failed with the exception which is the creator of this support ticket. (JNDIConnector fails to initialize)

Attempt [2]-> I get from GitHub notes (https://github.ibm.com/sec-di/adks/tree/sdi72/castor/0.9.5.4#readme) that we are not using castor file as-is which are downloaded. We are adding Marshaller & UnmarshalHandler classes into it. So now what I did is that in castor (0.9.5.4) version, I replaced vulnerable class of Xerces SAX Parser with non-vulnerable class got from castor (1.4.1) version.

This way we achieve both the goals ->

    Marshaller & UnmarshalHandler classes remain in-tact.
    Castor becomes non-vulnerable i.e. we fixed it.

About oro jar ->

We are using oro 2.0.8 library for the first time. https://mvnrepository.com/artifact/oro/oro/2.0.8

This library is pretty stable and old released in 2005 and no more vulnerability is reported on it as of today's date.

